HST Office: document tabs on macOS in native full screen stay clickable after "+", and a tab takes over
the window geometry in place (no 28 px jump on every new tab or tab switch).

Owner report (macOS 14.6.1, 1.0.4-rc.1, also in 1.0.3): in native full screen, the tab strip "+"
opened the new document, then nothing could be clicked (tab strip, ribbon, menu bar), not even
another tab; the event loop was idle (sample). macOS runner probe (NSWindow trace every 100 ms):
the new tab joined the native tab group of the full screen window, but the previous tab stayed the
group's selected window; when the tab group parked it, AquaSalFrame::Hide took it out of the group
(removeWindow + orderOut) and the new tab was left in a full screen Space that was no longer the
active one: keys still reached it, clicks did not.

- vcl/osx/salframe.cxx: joinNativeFullScreenTabs selects the new tab after addTabbedWindow. Hide asks
  the native group which window is selected instead of isVisible (the trace showed the replaced tab
  still visible while the new one was selected): a tab that is not selected is hidden by the
  selection and stays in the group; a tab that is still selected selects the other shown tab of its
  native group instead of leaving it; only without one it leaves and orders out as before.

Windowed (all platforms): DocumentTabGroup::copyGeometry gave the incoming tab the geometry of the
shown tab through SystemWindow::SetWindowState, whose #96568 check moves a frame placed exactly over
another shown frame by the title bar height (28 px on macOS), back to the top once off screen. The
shown tab is still there when its geometry is copied, so every new or switched-to tab moved
(macOS runner sampler: 102,65 -> 130,93 -> 158,121); maximized windows were exempt.

- vcl/source/window/syswin.cxx: hst_vcl_set_window_state_in_place (exported, declared in the
  framework like hst_vcl_set_tab_group): SetWindowState without the #96568 displacement.
- framework documenttabgroup.cxx: copyGeometry uses it. Detaching a tab into a window of its own
  keeps the cascade.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); the new test files are HST's
(LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary).
Test: CppunitTest_vcl_hst_window_state_in_place; macOS runner probe scripts/macos/fs-new-tab-probe.sh
(branch probe/mac-new-tab-hang).
